<task id="020" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-06: filename defaults to Document Name, editable in-pane</title>
    <phase>2 Save flow</phase>
    <gate>015 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .tsx/.ts client code AND the BFF save persistence path (sprk_documentname mapping); tags include frontend + bff-api.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified UI defaulting plus a single, precisely-located server field mapping. No architectural judgment required; the reference impl and the exact defect site are both named below.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-a</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>015</deps>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, bff-api, office-addins, save-flow, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the pane's "Document Name" field default to the document's filename and be editable in place via a pencil affordance, and make that edited value actually persist to the Dataverse `sprk_documentname` column. Today the user's typed name lands in `sprk_documentdescription` while `sprk_documentname` silently receives the sanitized SPE filename with `.docx` appended — that is the UAT defect this task closes.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in React 19 + Fluent UI v9 task-pane components, Office.js host adapters, and the BFF Office save persistence path into Dataverse. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>The Save tab shows a Document Name that is pre-filled from the filename, editable in-pane behind a pencil affordance, and whose final value is written to `sprk_documentname` (NVARCHAR(850)) on the created `sprk_document`. The SPE blob filename remains independently correct (`.docx`, sanitized). Contract test covers the mapping; unit tests cover the defaulting and edit behaviors.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-06 requires: the Document Name field defaults to the filename, is editable in-pane via a pencil affordance, edits persist to `sprk_documentname`, and the field can be removed from the Dataverse form without loss of the value.

      Verified as-built (do not re-derive):
      - `SaveFlow.tsx:423` initializes `documentName` to the empty string — there is no default at all today. `SaveFlow.tsx:849-860` renders it as an always-open `Textarea` labeled "Document Name" (no pencil affordance).
      - `useSaveFlow.ts:770` computes `effectiveDocumentName = context.documentName || context.itemName`, then `:852-853` forces a `.docx` suffix onto it to build `document.fileName`, and `:856` also sends it as `document.title`.
      - `useSaveFlow.ts:784-787` additionally sends a TOP-LEVEL `documentMetadata: {name, description}` object. `SaveRequest` has NO such member, so System.Text.Json silently drops it. This is dead weight on the wire and must be removed or made real as part of this task — do not leave a request field that no server member receives.
      - Server: `OfficeDocumentPersistence.CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync` builds `CreateDocumentRequest { Name = fileName, Description = request.Document?.Title ?? request.Document?.FileName }`. `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:277` maps `Name` to `sprk_documentname` and `:280` maps `Description` to `sprk_documentdescription`. So the user's Document Name currently reaches the DESCRIPTION column and the sanitized `.docx` filename reaches the NAME column — inverted.
      - `OfficeService.cs:408` sanitizes `request.Document.FileName` via `SpeUploadPath.SanitizeFileName` before it becomes the SPE upload path. That sanitization is load-bearing (it is the folder-minting fix) and must stay on the FILENAME, not on the display name.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/SaveView.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Office/SaveRequest.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/__tests__/SaveFlow.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="015" status="pending">FR-03 tab shell — the Save tab frame this field renders inside, and the `NavigationTab` extension that lets Word show tabs at all.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the display name and the SPE blob filename are TWO values, not one. Within this task: `sprk_documentname` receives the user-facing Document Name (unsanitized apart from length); the SPE upload path continues to receive the sanitized, `.docx`-suffixed filename via `SpeUploadPath.SanitizeFileName` at `OfficeService.cs:408`. MUST NOT collapse them back into one value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — `sprk_documentname` is NVARCHAR(850). Within this task, truncate or reject at 850 characters at the boundary that writes it; MUST NOT silently truncate to 200 the way `CommunicationService.cs` does for its own email paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — for the client request body only: remove the dead top-level `documentMetadata` object at `useSaveFlow.ts:784-787`, or add the matching server member. MUST NOT ship a request field that no `SaveRequest` member receives.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">SCOPE — any Dataverse GUID this task reads or writes (document id, target entity id) is canonicalized to bare-lowercase via the shared `cleanGuid` at every boundary. Never interpolate a raw GUID into an OData key predicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE — for all pane UI added or modified here: Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only, no hex literals, and the pencil/edit affordance must honor the Office light/dark theme via `useOfficeTheme`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE — for this add-in package only: per this project's Path A exception, keep the field UI as a thin view under `shared/taskpane/`. MUST NOT import `@spaarke/ui-components` components here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-03: `Xrm.*` does not exist in an Office host. MUST NOT import any Xrm-bound component (including the `Create*Wizard` family). Recreate the layout, per the r2 precedent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE — this task modifies the behavior of `POST /api/office/save`, so it MUST add or update a contract test in `tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs` asserting the name mapping. Cite `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` — there is no concise copy in `.claude/adr/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — BFF publish size: measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD OF `origin/master`, never against the recorded baseline number (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). Zip both with PowerShell `Compress-Archive` (the method `scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1` uses) and report both absolute sizes plus the delta and the tool name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the PR description MUST state the Placement Justification for every BFF-side change in this task, per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, even when the answer is "extends an existing route group".</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — run `/conflict-check` before opening any BFF-touching PR. `spaarkeai-compose-r8` and `unified-access-control-r2` are live on this same hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — build commands for `src/client/office-addins` only: install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; there is NO `build:prod` script — `npm run build` IS the production build.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Office add-in save flow, Fluent v9 in an Office host, Dataverse document field mapping</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/spec.md</file>
