    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-host-visual-fit" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md">Explicitly covers Office add-ins. Apply its density and token rules to the inline-edit affordance so the field does not overflow the narrow pane.</pattern>
      <pattern name="endpoint-filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Read before touching anything on the `/api/office` group; authorization stays on the filter, never in the handler body.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md, spec.md FR-06, and the knowledge files above. Output the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL) per root CLAUDE.md §8.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the four verified defect sites: SaveFlow.tsx:423 and :849-860, useSaveFlow.ts:770 / :784-787 / :852-856, and OfficeDocumentPersistence.CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync's CreateDocumentRequest construction. Confirm each still reads as described before changing it.</step>
    <step order="2">Client: derive the default Document Name from the filename. In Word, source it from the host adapter's document name/subject; in Outlook, from the subject. Strip the extension for display; keep the extension only on the wire filename.</step>
    <step order="3">Client: replace the always-open Document Name Textarea with a read-only display plus a pencil (edit) affordance that reveals an editable Input. Keep it keyboard-reachable and announce the state change via the existing `useAnnounce` pattern (NFR-11).</step>
    <step order="4">Client: separate the two wire values in `useSaveFlow.ts`. `document.fileName` keeps the `.docx` enforcement; `document.title` carries the user-facing Document Name. Remove the dead top-level `documentMetadata` object (or make it real — pick one and say which in the PR).</step>
    <step order="5">Server: in `OfficeDocumentPersistence`, map the user-facing name to `CreateDocumentRequest.Name` (which lands in `sprk_documentname`) and stop putting it in `Description`. Enforce the 850-character bound at this boundary.</step>
    <step order="6">Add/extend the contract test in `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs`: a Document save whose `document.title` differs from `document.fileName` results in `sprk_documentname` equal to the title, and the SPE filename equal to the sanitized `.docx` name.</step>
    <step order="7">Add unit tests in `shared/taskpane/components/__tests__/SaveFlow.test.tsx` covering: default population from the filename, the pencil toggling to edit, an edit surviving to the built save context, and the 850-character bound.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, and `npm run build` in `src/client/office-addins`; run `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests. All green.</step>
    <step order="9">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the constraint above. Record both absolute sizes, the delta, and the zip tool in the PR and in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check`, then code-review + adr-check per task-execute Step 9.5.</step>
    <step order="11">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If separating the display name from the SPE filename would change behavior for the Email or Attachment content types (whose names come from `OfficeEmailEnricher.GenerateEmlFileName`, not from user input), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than adapting. This change is scoped to `ContentType=Document`.</trigger>
    <trigger>If `sprk_documentname` turns out to be enforced shorter than 850 characters anywhere in the write path, STOP and escalate rather than silently truncating to the smaller bound.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Document Name defaults from the filename">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Word document named "Acme Merger Agreement.docx" and open the Spaarke pane on the Save tab.</step>
        <step>Observe the Document Name field without typing anything.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The field shows "Acme Merger Agreement" (no extension), read-only, with a pencil affordance beside it.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Pencil affordance edits in place and persists">
      <steps>
        <step>Click the pencil, change the value to "Acme Merger Agreement - Execution Copy", pick a related record, and Save.</step>
        <step>Open the resulting `sprk_document` record in Dataverse.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>`sprk_documentname` equals "Acme Merger Agreement - Execution Copy"; `sprk_documentdescription` is not populated with the name; the stored SPE file is named with a sanitized `.docx` filename.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode check via the Office theme toggle">
      <steps>
        <step>In Word, switch the Office theme to Dark (File, Account, Office Theme) and reload the pane.</step>
        <step>Inspect the Document Name field in both its read-only and editing states, including the pencil icon and focus ring.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Text, border, icon, and focus ring all resolve from Fluent v9 semantic tokens with legible contrast in dark mode; no hardcoded light-mode colors; repeat in Light mode with the same result.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Keyboard-only operation (NFR-11)">
      <steps>
        <step>Using only Tab/Shift+Tab/Enter/Escape, reach the pencil affordance, enter edit mode, change the value, and commit.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Every state is reachable and operable by keyboard; the transition into and out of edit mode is announced via `useAnnounce`.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF and run the Office contract tests.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Install with --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; typecheck, test, and build (build IS production here).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/__tests__/SaveFlow.test.tsx</output>
