  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Word document opened in the pane, when the Save tab renders, then the Document Name field is pre-populated with the document's filename minus its extension.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the pre-populated Document Name, when the user clicks the pencil affordance, then the field becomes editable in-pane and the change is announced via `useAnnounce`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an edited Document Name, when the save completes, then `sprk_documentname` on the created `sprk_document` equals the edited value exactly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an edited Document Name, when the save completes, then the SPE blob filename is the sanitized value with a `.docx` extension and is NOT overwritten by the display name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Document Name longer than 850 characters, when the user saves, then the value is bounded to 850 characters at the write boundary and the save succeeds rather than throwing an unhandled Dataverse length error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a Document Name left empty, when the user saves, then the save still succeeds using the filename-derived default, and `sprk_documentname` is never empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the request body sent to `POST /api/office/save` contains no top-level `documentMetadata` object with no corresponding `SaveRequest` member; verified by inspecting the serialized body in the `useSaveFlow` unit test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Office theme set to Dark, when the pane renders, then every color in the Document Name field resolves from a Fluent v9 semantic token and no hex literal appears in the modified styles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A contract test in `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs` asserts the title-to-`sprk_documentname` mapping and is executing (not `[Fact(Skip)]`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean for the files this task touched; `npm test` and `npm run build` pass; `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size is measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive`, both absolute sizes and the delta are recorded, and the delta is under the +5 MB escalation threshold.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-06; plan.md §4 Phase 2 task 020. The inverted name/description mapping is the concrete UAT complaint — the record list shows `.docx` filenames instead of the names users typed. The "field can be removed from the Dataverse form without loss" acceptance in FR-06 follows automatically once the value is written to the column rather than being form-only.
  </notes>

